# Copy to .env.local for local development.
# Every var here must also exist in the ARCHITECTURE.md table and the Vercel
# project config, added in the same commit as the code that reads it.

# Supabase project "pulse" (eu-west-2). Never point this at the retainer
# dashboard or the old Pulse Recruit project.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxx

# Absolute origin. Needed in deployed environments so auth redirects land on
# the right host. Leave unset locally.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://pulse.recruitergtm.io

# --- Platform AI keys (AI.md section 1) -------------------------------------
# These are RecruiterGTM's own keys, not the customer's. One central account,
# every org spends against it, credits are the cost control. Server only: never
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, never read outside src/lib/server/ai/.
# Check them with: npm run verify:ai
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxx
EXA_API_KEY=xxx

# Optional. Changing the model means updating MODEL_RATES in
# src/lib/server/ai/pricing.ts in the same commit, or the credit meter lies.
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o

# --- LinkedIn posting through Unipile (Pillar 5) ----------------------------
# RecruiterGTM holds ONE Unipile tenant. Recruiters never see a key: they
# authorise their LinkedIn profile through Unipile's hosted wizard and it
# becomes an account under our tenant. So these are platform vars, not per-org
# Vault keys, and Unipile is not on the API keys screen.
# Billing is roughly 5 EUR per connected account per month on a 49 EUR minimum,
# charged on the peak count in a 30 day window, so a forgotten account costs
# real money.
UNIPILE_API_KEY=xxx
UNIPILE_DSN=https://apiXX.unipile.com:XXXXX

# Unipile does not sign its callbacks, so this secret travels in the notify URL
# we mint and /api/unipile/accounts compares it in constant time. Generate with
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. Changing it invalidates links already sent.
UNIPILE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=xxx

# The Unipile callback arrives with no user session, so there is nobody for an
# RLS policy to check. This is the one caller of the service-role client, in
# src/lib/server/supabase-admin.ts. Never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, never imported
# by a client component.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=xxx

# --- Per-org integration keys are NOT env vars ------------------------------
# Instantly, HeyReach, Beehiiv and custom SMTP are the customer's own accounts.
# Each org pastes its own key into Settings and it is stored encrypted in
# Supabase Vault, so it can be rotated per customer without a deploy. See
# ARCHITECTURE.md and AI.md.
